item.p:
audits which in accordance with Article. 24, paragraph 1 letter a of the Financial Market Supervision Act of 22 June 2007
SR 956.1 (FINMASA) or Article 118i of the Collective Investment Schemes Act of 23 June 2006
SR 951.31 (CISA) must be conducted by a licensed audit company for regulatory audits;

guarantee compliance with statutory provisions

  Expression according to paragraph I of the FA of 20 June 2014 (Bundling of Audit Oversight), in force since 1 Jan. 2015 (AS 2014 4073; BBl 2013 6857). The change was made throughout the entire text.
	;

does not exercise any other activity subject to licensing in accordance with the financial market acts (Article 1 paragraph 1 FINMASA

  SR 956.1
	).

blockList.listIntroduction:
 In addition to the general statutory provisions on the independence of auditors (Article 728 CO

 SR 220
	), audit firms under state oversight must observe the following principles when providing audit services to public interest entities:

item.p:
audit companies and lead auditors for the audit under the financial market acts (Article 1 paragraph 1 FINMASA

  SR 956.1
	) in accordance with Article 9a.

Articles 146, 152, 153, 161, 166, 251, 253–255 and 321 of the Swiss Criminal Code

 SR 311.0
	;

Article 47 of the Banking Act of 8 November 1934

 SR 952.0
	;

Article 69 of the Financial Institutions Act of 15 June 2018

 SR 954.1
	;

content.p:
The cantonal civil courts and the Federal Supreme Court shall notify the Oversight Authority of all proceedings relating to auditors’ liability (Article 755 CO

 SR 220
	) that are connected with an auditing service provided by an audit firm under state oversight. They shall supply it with the judgments and other decisions that conclude such proceedings.

item.p:
the principles of independence in accordance with Articles 11 and 728 of the CO

 SR 220
	;

failing to comply with the duties to document and retain records as an audit firm under state oversight (Art. 730c CO

 SR 220
	);

content.p:
 The Oversight Authority takes over all proceedings from FINMA which were initiated against audit companies performing audits under the financial market acts (Article 1 paragraph 1 FINMASA

 SR 956.1
	) as well as against lead auditors of such audits and which by the enactment of the amendment of 20 June 2014 have not yet been legally decided.
